sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-argonauta-argo-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-argonauta-argo-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-argonauta-argo-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Argonauta argo Schnakenberg critical mode at the 95 µm Holocene tier — MorphoEval overall 81.3/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 1 judges the smooth critical-mode animation (12 frames, 800×600). Schnakenberg parameters a=0.10, b=0.90, D_u=1, D_v=18 give trace=-0.2, det=1, k_c=0.610, σ(k_c)=0.200, and equal-diffusion σ_max=-0.100. The plate's radial profile matches the mode at Pearson r=0.99934 (RMSE 0.00550). Measured inhibitory halo is 85.87 µm against the 95 µm tier label. Smooth-control image CV against the plate is 80.2. Overall 81.3/100. Grain amplitude, grained coherency, and a second assessor are still open. Overall 81.3/100 (faithfulness 79.9, reproducibility 84.8); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0e502ec97af571f7d94f76469868477feaaf61eb; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 84, Morphological realism / specimen match 74, Parameter expressivity 86, Morphometric validation 80, Source and data traceability 88, Code-to-model traceability 82, Reproducibility package 84. Output judged: datasets/argonauta_argo_turing_wavelength_s0/argonauta_argo_turing_wavelength_s0_smooth_control.gif: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-argonauta-argo-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0e502ec97af571f7d94f76469868477feaaf61eb, image/gif, 658416 B, 800×600 px, 12 frames, artifact_sha256 23ce19963dbc42f1b0b7e9b93a3c6f7bd90edf6deb9742f57a8a4a5d2c94b940 (sha256 23ce19963dbc42f1b0b7e9b93a3c6f7bd90edf6deb9742f57a8a4a5d2c94b940), spec_fingerprint 54b806e24537aefcedcf7233858405c3246c56ac09b2d0e212f862aff5e91fe3. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 54b806e24537aefcedcf7233858405c3246c56ac09b2d0e212f862aff5e91fe3; artifact_sha256: 23ce19963dbc42f1b0b7e9b93a3c6f7bd90edf6deb9742f57a8a4a5d2c94b940; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/argonauta_argo_turing_wavelength_s0/argonauta_argo_shell_cc0.jpg=b3b1284cdbe9512b..., datasets/argonauta_argo_turing_wavelength_s0/argonauta_argo_turing_wavelength_s0_specimen.jpg=4d2cfc3367b264b3..., datasets/argonauta_argo_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=97c63e114209a765...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing (1952) selects a finite critical wavenumber when the inhibitor out-diffuses the activator and the reaction Jacobian is stable without diffusion. | Gierer & Meinhardt (1972) produce spots by local activation and long-range inhibition. | Finn & Norman (2010) describe the female Argonauta argo brood shell as a buoyancy organ.; reconstructed_in_script: A radial critical mode whose period is the plate's peak-to-peak spacing (170.03 µm) and whose halo (85.87 µm) is compared with the 95 µm tier. | The length unit (16.51 µm) that places analytical k_c on that measured period.; transfer_boundary: Kondo & Asai (1995) is a pigment reaction-diffusion wave in a fish, not a measurement on Argonauta.; does_not_claim: Finn & Norman did not measure a 95 µm Turing wavelength. | The gallery plate is not a raw camera micrograph and is not one of their figures. | Diffusivities are not independently measured chemical constants. | There is no sampled predecessor chronospecies; none is invented.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: R1: Sweep procedural grain amplitude and keep the value that raises CV similarity of the growth GIF; the smooth control scores 80.2.",
            "remediation needed: R2: Recompute structure-tensor coherency on the grained frame. The smooth field's coherency (0.998) is not comparable to the plate (0.203).",
            "remediation needed: R3: Independent second assessor. This round is builder-scored.",
            "remediation needed: R4: Nanopublication signing. ~/.nanopub/profile.yml is not present; do not invent a signature.",
            "remediation needed: R5: The pattern target is one gallery plate (n=1), not a population of Argonauta ocelli." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.813"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (builder-assessor, single-agent round; second assessor not run)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> .
}

